      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Surgeons perform total shoulder arthroplasty (TSA) procedures to reduce patients' intractable arthritic pain and to repair humeral head fractures. Total shoulder arthroplasty has undergone remarkable advances--not only in prosthetic improvements and refinements--but in patient outcomes. Advantages to TSA procedures include decreased pain and patients' increased ability to perform activities of daily living."},
